<metadata><name>Pocket Creek Trail (Pocket Creek Sno-Park to the Upper Junction)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:204-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park (OSM node 6287637025); confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 3800; quote: From Pocket Creek Sno-Park, 13 miles around Hood from Government Camp, ski east on the almost level road 0.6 mile to a bridge crossing of the East Fork</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302220" lon="-121.603446"><ele>1288.4</ele><name>Upper Junction</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Road 3540 and Forest Road 3540-640 (the upper Pocket Creek road, going south); Meadows Creek Trail joins 60 m east; 2.65 mi along Road 3540 from the pin; DEM 4,227 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: follow the road up the east side of the valley on a gentle climb through alternating forest and clearcuts to a road junction, hereafter referred to as the "Upper Junction," 2.7 miles from the trailhead</desc></wpt>
